node_modules/

# The codemod-rows gate reads its maps from the INSTALLED @noy-db/hub, so its
# fixture needs a real resolvable node_modules/@noy-db/hub. It is a committed
# relative symlink to the sibling fixture package, not an installed tree — the
# blanket node_modules/ rule above would swallow it.
!tools/fixtures/workspace/packages/a/node_modules/

# Same reason, for the prose-examples gate: `at` measured (family#26) that a
# flat workspace has no hoisted @noy-db/* at the repo root, so the gate compiles
# each README INSIDE its owning package and the fixture must therefore resolve
# its own package name from there. Another committed relative symlink.
# ⛔ Without this line the fixture's node_modules is swallowed, the tests still
# pass LOCALLY against the developer's working copy, and CI fails on a checkout
# that never had the link — the ignored-file-the-tests-depend-on trap.
!tools/fixtures/workspace-prose/packages/lib/node_modules/
